\pard\sa160\f0\fs22 Before a customer session, run the {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "file:///home/syazwan/github/paf26.7_livelab/docs/livelab/files/test-prompts.md"}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf2 24 validation prompts}}}, record pass/partial/fail privately and compare key answers with the SQLcl verification results. Confirm identity, storage ordering, blocker scope, the exact job window, cumulative SQL interpretation, and a complete overall-health answer. Test invalid input and unrelated questions as well as successful queries.\par
\pard\sa160\f0\fs22 The September implementation reports document a baseline and targeted instruction retests; the full suite was not rerun after the final overall-health adjustment. The {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "file:///home/syazwan/github/paf26.7_livelab/docs/livelab-paf-only/README.md"}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf2 PAF-only workshop}}} also records a 28 September overnight-report clarification failure. Treat clarification as an acceptance test, not a guaranteed behavior. See the {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "file:///home/syazwan/github/paf26.7_livelab/tests/paf/results-monitoring-agent-2026-09-24.md"}{\fldrslt{\ul\cf2 Agent test report}}}.\par
\pard\sa160\f0\fs22 {\f1 COLLECTED_AT_UTC} is calculated when queried, not stored history. Use Scheduler event timestamps for job windows. Tablespace metrics, retained runs and cumulative SQL counters support bounded observations; they do not establish a complete root cause or continuous service health. This demo provides conversational, on-demand checks, not scheduled monitoring or alerts.\par
\pard\sa160\f0\fs22 The views are read-only, but the login retains underlying SELECT and cloud-package privileges. Agent instructions express intended behavior and are not a hard authorization boundary. Do not present this configuration as a hardened production monitoring service.\par
